<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrei of Gorodets</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1304</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Andrei III of Vladimir, Andrei Alexandrovich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrei of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorodets">Gorodets</a> (Andrei Alexandrovich) was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a> and grand prince of Vladimir in the early 1280s and from 1294 to 1304. His long feud with his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-of-pereslavl">Dmitry of Pereslavl</a>, each backed by a rival Mongol power, brought repeated Horde armies into north-eastern Rus', most destructively in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dudenevs-raid">Dudenev's raid</a> of 1293. He also ruled Novgorod at times and held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of Gorodets.</p></div>
